# Deployment identity.
#
# One blog per folder is the normal case, but two checkouts of this template on
# one machine is the *documented* workflow (the template repo plus your own
# site), and `docker compose up` in both would otherwise build into the same
# `archive-blog:local` image tag and fight over the same `archive-blog`
# container name — the second `up` silently replaces the first.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and set a name per checkout:
#
#   BLOG_NAME=my-site
#   BLOG_PORT=8081
#
# Left unset, everything falls back to the template's own defaults, so every
# command in the docs keeps working verbatim.
BLOG_NAME=archive-blog
BLOG_PORT=4322
